distance":0.6601,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Liam Coen"}],"defense":[{"season":2023,"team":"PIT","distance":0.2338,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"GB","distance":0.4299,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"CLE","distance":0.4932,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"HOU","distance":0.5435,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"NO","distance":0.5581,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Dennis Allen"}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Jaguars are 6-2 through week 9 of the 2026 season and have outscored opponents 229 to 121. Both sides of the ball have been strong, with the offense 2nd in EPA per play and the defense 3rd in EPA allowed. What sets them apart is the 2nd highest eight man box rate in the league.","offense":"The Jaguars have one of the most efficient offenses in the league so far, ranking in the top eight in all five main efficiency measures. Their run and pass mix has stayed close to what game situations call for. Trevor Lawrence has run the passing game and leaned heavily on Parker Washington, who has drawn 26% of the targets.","defense":"The Jaguars have one of the best defenses in the league this season, ranking 3rd or better in four of the five main efficiency measures. Its strongest area has been EPA allowed per play, where it ranks 3rd, and its weakest has been sack rate, where it ranks 20th. Josh Hines-Allen has led the way with 2 sacks. In terms of scheme, they have the 2nd highest eight man box rate in the league.","special":"The Jaguars have been one of the most conservative teams on fourth down, going for it on only 14% of their short-yardage chances. Their kickers have made 88% of field goals, which is about average. Their salary cap was spread across positions in a fairly typical way.","players":"Trevor Lawrence has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 1,932 yards. Parker Washington has been the clear top target with 26% of the looks and 493 receiving yards. Bhayshul Tuten has handled most of the work in the backfield with 60% of the carries. On defense, Travon Walker leads the team with 3 sacks and Jourdan Lewis has picked off 3 passes.","coaching":"Liam Coen is calling the offense as head coach and Anthony Campanile is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2023 Lions under Ben Johnson and the 2023 Browns under Kevin Stefanski. Their defense looks most like the 2023 Steelers and the 2023 Packers.","trends":"The offense went from 14th in EPA per play in 2025 to 2nd so far this season, a big step forward. The defense moved from 3rd in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 3rd so far this season, about where it was. The biggest change in approach was eight man box rate, which went from 5% to 13%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}